From 8f279958de8ac5d8909ae3bf4df608a7ac9731b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Uwe Augustin <Info@FlapsOnline.de>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:49:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] SystemdConfigPanel: the OpenVario system functions
 below the services

On an OpenVario, XCSoar is started from the menu of the image, and
until now a pilot had to quit to that menu to calibrate the sensors or
to switch the device over to OpenSoar.  These functions belong
together with sensord and variod, which the "Services" page
already controls, so they appear on that page below the service list
instead of on a page of their own; the configuration dialog has
enough pages already.  The page also shows which image the device is
running, which is the first thing to know when reporting a problem.

The part is only added when /boot/config.uEnv exists, so a desktop
Linux machine sees the page as before.  The choice of the program to
start after boot is written to that file when the dialog closes, like
every other setting, and ovmenu-ng.sh reads it at the next boot.

When config.uEnv names no program, the selection shows the running
one, because the image has evidently started it; the comparison
ignores the case, as the start script does.
